{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jaciatqduqjqv4vahuzacpurcwxwki3xtb44vivm273ftlbgdxhq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four phases are complete. Summary:\n\n## Phase A — both build and run\n- **C:** `cd c_src && mkdir -p build && cd build && cmake .. && cmake --build .` → run as `./driver <base> <exponent>`\n- **Rust:** `cd translation && cargo build --release` → `target/release/driver <base> <exponent>`\n- Both compiled with no errors (the Rust crate needed no fixes).\n\n## Phase B — differential tests\n`translation/tests/differential.rs` — 25 tests, each exec'ing **both binaries as subprocesses** and comparing stdout, stderr *and* exit status. Key harness detail: `argv[0]` appears in the usage message, so both are exec'd with a fixed `argv[0]` via `CommandExt::arg0` — otherwise the differing binary paths would produce a fake mismatch.\n\nCovered every branch in `main.c`: the `argc != 3` path (0/1/3/4 args, plus `argc == 0` via raw `execv`), both `ERANGE` checks, both `*endptr != '\\0'` checks, check *ordering*, `pow`'s `EDOM` and `ERANGE` paths, and the success path.\n\n## Phase C — the untried inputs\nSince happy-path passing proves little, I hunted mismatches with ~50 000 ad-hoc differential cases (random argument shapes, raw byte soup, exact-decimal sweeps around `2^-1074`/`2^-1022`/`DBL_MAX`, a `pow` cliff grid, `%.2f` tie cases). **No output mismatch was ever found — the translation is correct.**\n\nSo I validated the *suite* by mutation testing: 26 mutations injected into the Rust source one at a time. Four survived, exposing real coverage gaps that I then closed with C-verified inputs:\n\n| Uncovered branch | Input needed |\n|---|---|\n| exact-subnormal `ERANGE` exemption | `k·5^1074` + `e-1074` (~750-digit exact literal) |\n| the `2^-1022 − 2^-1076` underflow threshold | `(2^54−1)·5^1076 e-1076`, and that value ±1 in the last digit |\n| hex ties-to-even | `0x20000000000001p10` — scaled so one ulp shows through `%.2f` |\n| \"tiny but rounds up to `DBL_MIN`\" hex shortcut | `0x1.fffffffffffffffp-1023` |\n\nA fifth (exponent-saturation cap) survived even 700-digit mantissas; it only becomes observable past ~9 600 significant digits, so the suite now uses 10 000- and 20 000-digit arguments. Final score: **25/26 killed**; the lone survivor is a provably equivalent mutant (its assignment is discarded by the next statement), documented as such rather than papered over.\n\nFindings are recorded in `translation/ERRORS.md`, including the C behaviours that had to be replicated rather than fixed — notably that **an empty argument is silently accepted as `0.0`** (`strtod(\"\")` leaves `endptr` on the NUL, so the validation passes), while `\" \"` is rejected.\n\n## Phase D — gate\nBoth build clean; `cargo test` passes in debug **and** release (25/25); nothing `#[ignore]`d or skipped; `assert_same` additionally refuses to pass when the C program produced no output at all, so a mutually-silent pair can't masquerade as a match. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified — the only write under it is the `c_src/build/` cmake output from the instructed build command, and the test suite falls back to its own out-of-source build under `translation/target/c_build` if that's absent (verified by temporarily moving it aside and restoring it byte-identically). Scratch scripts were removed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2115,"cache_read_input_tokens":107220,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2115,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7507347f-a3c4-487e-9901-385ddd2daa38","uuid":"1bdad105-7b44-402c-aff4-a6903c64ec51","timestamp":"2026-08-28T10:39:13.674Z"}
